   "subject": "Splitting a chromosome into two",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">I am looking for R code to split a chromosome.<br></blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">My chromosome 2 is too large and it is affecting the view of  the distribution  of other markers on other  chromosomes.</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"> </blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">So far I have found these, but not sure it this is right and they are not working.<blockquote><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">dataCNA$chrom&lt;- splitChromosomes(dataCNA$chrom,dataCNA$maploc) #splits the chromosomes into arms<br></span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">unlist(strsplit(&quot;chr2&quot;)</font></blockquote></blockquote><div><span style=\"line-height:18px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:18px\">The simplest thing would be to use a for loop, calling <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">movemarker()</font> repeatedly.</span><br></div>\r\n<p>Here&#39;s an example: for the hyper data, say I want to split chr 4 into chr 4a and chr 4b.<br></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"> data(hyper)<br></span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"> mnames &lt;- markernames(hyper, chr=4)<br></span></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"></span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"> # names of first half of markers, and their positions<br></span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"> firsthalf &lt;- mnames[1:(length(mnames)/2)]<br></span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"> pos &lt;- pull.map(hyper)[[4]][firsthalf]<br></span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"line-height:18px\"><br></span></font><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"> # move these markers to a chr &quot;4a&quot;, at same position as before<br></span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"> for(i in 1:length(firsthalf))<br></span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\">   hyper &lt;- movemarker(hyper, firsthalf[i], &quot;4a&quot;, pos[i])<br></span></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"></span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"> # rename chr 4 as chr &quot;4b&quot;<br></span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"> names(hyper$geno)[4] &lt;- &quot;4b&quot;<br></span></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"></span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;line-height:18px\"> # reorder chromosomes</span><p><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> hyper$geno &lt;- hyper$geno[c(1:3, &quot;4a&quot;, &quot;4b&quot;, 5:19, &quot;X&quot;)] </font></p></blockquote><div><div> karl</div></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</div></div>"
